course: dictionary
lesson: 3256
title: Equal and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word equal has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. In «Split the cake into equal parts», equal means the same in size. In «All people are equal», it means having the same rights.
explain: In maths, equals is a sign. The sign = means «is the same as», so 3 + 4 equals 7. The numbers and the sum tell you it is maths, not a talk about fairness.
explain: Chatty speakers say «fifty-fifty» or «split it even» when they mean equal shares. A formal text might use words like «equivalent» or «in equal proportion» for the same idea. Read the clues to check the meaning.
fact: Equal means the same in size, number or amount.
fact: Equal can also mean having the same rights and being treated the same way.
fact: «Equals» (=) means «is the same as», as in 3 + 4 equals 7.
fact: «Equal parts» are all the same size: a third means splitting a whole into equal parts and taking one part.
fact: Casual words for equal shares include «fifty-fifty» and «split it even».
exercise: «The Ukrainian constitution describes the flag as two equal stripes, blue above and yellow below.» What does equal mean here? | *Both stripes are the same size | Both stripes are different colours | One stripe is bigger than the other | The stripes are very thin
exercise: In maths, «3 + 4 equals 7». What does equals mean? | Is bigger than | Is next to | *Is the same as | Is taken away from
exercise: Your friend says, «Split it even.» What does she mean? | *Share it into equal parts | Give it all away to someone else | Keep it all for herself | Throw half of it away
test: «All people are equal.» What does equal mean here? | Being the same height as each other | Being the tallest in the class | *Having the same rights and being treated the same way | Being good at sport
test: «She equalled the school record.» What does equalled mean? | Broke the record by a long way | Forgot the record | Lost the record card | *Was as good as the record
exam: A formal text says the parts are «in equal proportion». What does this mean? | *In the same amount | In a very large amount | In a secret way | In a strange order
